# Demo UI/UX quality checklist

These apply to the `demo/` playground (Tailwind). They do not apply to the library in `src/`, which ships plain CSS. For deeper design guidance, use the `ui-ux-pro-max` skill in `.cursor/skills/` (requires Python).

## Icons & visual elements
- Use SVG icons (Lucide) - never emojis as UI icons.
- Consistent icon sizing (e.g. `h-4 w-4` / `h-5 w-5`); decorative icons get `aria-hidden="true"`.

## Interaction & cursor
- Every clickable/hoverable control has `cursor-pointer`.
- Hover feedback via color/opacity/border transitions - avoid layout-shifting scale transforms.
- Transitions are smooth: `transition-colors duration-200` (150-300ms). Not instant, not sluggish (>500ms).
- Visible keyboard focus states (`focus-visible:outline` or ring).

## Contrast & color
- Body text contrast >= 4.5:1. On dark backgrounds prefer `text-slate-100` / `text-slate-300`; avoid `text-slate-500` for body copy.
- Color is not the only indicator - pair color with text/labels.

## Layout & spacing
- Consistent container max-width.
- Responsive at 375 / 768 / 1024 / 1440 px; no horizontal scroll on mobile.

## Motion
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (the library already does; the demo must not force motion on top of it).

## Pre-delivery
- [ ] No emojis as icons
- [ ] All interactive elements have `cursor-pointer` + focus states
- [ ] Sufficient text contrast
- [ ] Responsive, no horizontal scroll
